.nh
.TH "PB-SESSION-PARTICIPANTS" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-session-participants - Show terminal sharing and connected participants


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb session participants <session-id> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Show terminal sharing and connected participants

.PP
Show current participants and sharing grants for one session. Use this to review access before removing a teammate or ending sharing.

.PP
Terminal sessions persist independently of a single connection and can be reattached after a disconnect. Sharing grants explicit access to a named session. Closing, deleting, and removing a participant have different effects; inspect the selected session before acting.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for participants

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print canonical JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-session(1)\fP
